2026-08-23 · No completions and no suggestions in the box
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Reported: the framed box offered neither. Two independent causes, and either
alone was enough.

1. THE COMPLETER WAS NEVER PASSED. `_dispatch_turn_framed` had built the app
   with `completer=SlashCommandCompleter(workspace)`; when that was replaced by
   the session-scoped `_start_frame`, the argument did not come with it. The
   buffer therefore had `complete_while_typing=False` and no completer at all.

2. THERE WAS NOWHERE TO DRAW ONE. `PromptSession` builds the completions menu
   for you - a `Float` anchored to the cursor. A hand-made `Layout` does not.
   So even with a completer the completions would have been computed and had
   no home. `FloatContainer` + `CompletionsMenu(max_height=12)` now wraps the
   HSplit.

Both are the same underlying mistake: a `PromptSession` is not just a `Buffer`,
and hand-rolling the layout means hand-rolling what it gave you for free. The
box also had no history suggestions for the same reason, so
`AutoSuggestFromHistory` went on at the same time.

Keys, matching the idle prompt so the two boxes behave alike:

    Tab / Shift-Tab   next / previous completion, opening the menu if closed
    Enter             accept the highlighted completion, else submit
    Right             accept the ghost suggestion at end-of-line, else move
    Alt-Enter         new line

Verified against the real Application over pipe input:

    typed "/qu"  -> ['/queue', '/queue add ', '/queue clear']
    Tab          -> '/queue' selected
    history "fix the failing tests", typed "fix the"
                 -> suggestion " failing tests", Right accepts it

    tests/test_tui.py   75 passed  (was 72)

    test_the_box_completes_slash_commands
    test_the_layout_has_somewhere_to_draw_completions
        asserts the FloatContainer and the CompletionsMenu exist - cause 2 on
        its own is invisible to a test that only checks the completer.
    test_the_box_suggests_from_what_you_typed_before


